  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c300.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 302.12 Compressed Natural Gas (CNG)",
  "priorExpiration": "2015-06-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 302.12 “Compressed Natural Gas (CNG)” means a natural gas compressed to a pressure at or above 200-248 bar, that is, 2900-3600 pounds per square inch, and stored in high-pressure containers. It is used as a fuel for natural gas-powered vehicles.\n\nSource. #10753, INTERIM, eff 1-1-15, EXPIRED: 6-30-15\n\nNew. #10890, eff 7-16-15; ss by #13186, eff 4-7-21 (formerly Saf-C 302.10) (See Revision Note #3 at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 300)",
